<script>
import DealNotes from 'crm/src/deals/lib/DealNotes.abide'
import dealNotesSource from 'crm/src/deals/lib/DealNotes.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import dealNotesTestSource from 'crm/src/deals/lib/DealNotes.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }

import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Registry from '#src/lib/Registry.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc>
    <Section title="A handler file answers at its own path">
        <p>A file named <code>&lt;name&gt;.handler.ts</code> beside the pages is a handler file. Its
            default export is the handler, and its path below <code>src</code> is the address it answers on.</p>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>File below <code>src</code></th><th>Answers on</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>**/&lt;name&gt;.handler.ts</code></td><td>its directory's route, then <code>&lt;name&gt;</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>deals/getDeal.handler.ts</code></td><td><code>GET /deals/getDeal</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>users/getUser.handler.ts</code></td><td><code>GET /users/getUser</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>health.handler.ts</code></td><td><code>GET /health</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>media/[id]/save.handler.ts</code></td><td><code>POST /media/42/save</code>, with <code>id</code> in its args</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>media/[id]/lib/Comments.abide</code></td><td><code>/__abide/handlers/media/id/lib/Comments/addComment</code>, for the <code>addComment</code> its <code>&lt;script server&gt;</code> declares</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>A handler file exports its handler and nothing else. A page imports it, a script calls
            its address, and the CLI and MCP offer it as a command and a tool.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="A handler only one file calls stays in that file">
        <Example
            id="notes"
            app="crm"
            title="`const getNotes = GET(fn)` — a handler its own file calls"
            summary="The notes on a deal, which only this card shows. The handler sits in the card's own server block."
            files={{
                'src/deals/lib/DealNotes.abide': dealNotesSource,
                'src/deals/lib/DealNotes.test.ts': dealNotesTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <DealNotes />
        </Example>

        <p>A <code>&lt;script server&gt;</code> runs on the server alone. It declares
            <code>getNotes</code> as a <code>const</code>, and the same file's script and markup call it
            by name. A <code>.abide</code> exports nothing, so no other file can import it.</p>

        <p>It still answers over http, below <code>/__abide/handlers</code> at its file's path and
            then its name. That address is listed on no surface, and the test calls it to show it is
            there. When a second file needs the handler, move it into a handler file:
            <code>const getNotes =</code> becomes <code>export default</code>.</p>
    </Section>

    <Registry />
</Doc>
